I didn't import this answer because of two blockers, and I haven't written anything.

1. **I can't open the link.** There's no web-reading tool in this session. I tried a sub-agent, and it had no web access either, so no request ever reached Zhihu. Zhihu answers also often sit behind a login wall or anti-bot check, so a fetcher might not have worked anyway. I haven't summarized the post from memory or guessed at it.
2. **I couldn't find your personal knowledge folder.** There's no `./knowledge/` folder here and no `knowledge_path:` line in a `CLAUDE.md`. I also can't check whether `$TRADE_KNOWLEDGE_DIR` is set. That folder is where the digest would go (never the public `references/` library).

**To continue, send me:**
- **The content**, in one of these forms:
  - the answer text pasted into chat;
  - a PDF ("print to PDF" from the page);
  - screenshots (`.png` / `.jpg`);
  - or a session with web access and a working `opencli-reader`.
- **Your knowledge folder's path.** If you don't have one yet, run `/trade setup` first.

Once I have both, I'll write a digest in English at `<knowledge>/writedowns/2026-09-28-<topic>.md`. It will include:
- who wrote it and where it came from, with a note that its data isn't independently checked;
- a short summary and the main argument;
- signs to watch that would show whether the thesis is playing out;
- the bear case, and what would prove it wrong;
- trading implications, clearly marked as my view rather than the author's.

If it's a macro piece, I'll also score it against the seven-stage framework. I'll keep a copy of the original source in a separate raw-sources folder so the digest can be re-checked later.

